.TH DHCPIG\-WEB 1 "2026-08-01" "dhcpig 2.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dhcpig\-web \- local web interface for the DHCPig network-hardening validator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhcpig\-web
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dhcpig\-web
serves a local, single-page control plane for
.BR dhcpig (1).
It drives the same engine as the command line tool: the modes, safety
behaviour and findings are identical, and every run is reported through a
live event log with a session report available as JSON, CSV or HTML.
.PP
The server is written against the Python standard library only \- there is no
web framework, no build step and no remote asset of any kind, and the content
security policy forbids remote origins.
.PP
It is not a system service. Nothing is registered with systemd, no port is
opened at boot, and the process listens only while it is running in the
foreground. Raw socket access (root) is required for a run to send anything,
so it is normally started with
.BR sudo (8)
or
.BR pkexec (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDRESS"
Address to listen on. Defaults to
.BR 127.0.0.1 ,
the loopback address. Binding anywhere else exposes the control plane of a
Layer-2 attack tool to the network and prints a warning; to reach the
interface from another machine, prefer forwarding the loopback port over SSH
.RI ( "ssh \-L 8787:127.0.0.1:8787 host" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port to listen on. Default
.BR 8787 .
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the system browser at the tokenized URL once the server is listening.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
A random token is generated at startup and printed on stdout as part of the
URL. Every request must carry it, either as a
.I token
query parameter or an
.B Authorization: Bearer
header, and requests carrying an
.B Origin
header from a different host are rejected. The token is not persisted; it
changes on every start.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
The interface can start disruptive runs. The same warnings as for
.BR dhcpig (1)
apply: only use it against networks you own or are explicitly authorised to
test.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcpig (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Kevin Amorin
